</p></sec><sec><title id="SEC3.6">Other targets</title><p>Ideal targets for oncological therapeutics should be expressed at high levels on the surface of neoplastic cells while remaining absent in normal cells. However, the majority of promising targets exhibit microexpression in common tissues. As formerly described, we have delineated several targets with substantial clinical potential.
<xref rid="TBL6" ref-type="table">Tables 6</xref> and
<xref rid="TBL7" ref-type="table">7</xref> offer a synopsis of some alternative targets.
